    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Sunbaked Canyon over a fetch land means the player will take 1 life each time they tap it for mana going forward, while a fetch land would cost 1 life once and provide a permanent painless mana source. Additionally, saving Sunbaked Canyon for later preserves the option to sacrifice it for card draw when running low on resources.",
