      "decision_index": 59,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Phelia before combat and before using Stoneforge Mystic's activated ability is suboptimal sequencing. The player has Stoneforge Mystic available to put an Equipment (Batterskull, Cryptic Coat, or Pre-War Formalwear) directly onto the battlefield. Specifically, activating Stoneforge to put Batterskull into play would create a 4/4 vigilance lifelink Germ token immediately, which is a much stronger board development. Phelia could then be cast post-combat or next turn. Additionally, casting Phelia in the precombat main phase rather than using her flash ability means the opponent gets full information before deciding blocks. More importantly, the opponent has Karakas on the battlefield, which can bounce legendary Phelia back to hand, potentially wasting the mana spent casting her.",
