      "action_taken": "Played Wasteland as land drop before casting Brainstorm or activating Stoneforge Mystic",
      "better_line": "Cast Brainstorm first (using Tundra for {U}), see three new cards, put two back, then decide whether to play Wasteland or hold it, and then activate Stoneforge Mystic to put Batterskull or Cryptic Coat onto the battlefield",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 67,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 100,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The Phyrexian Germ token equipped with Batterskull is a 4/4 with vigilance and lifelink. Since it has vigilance, it stays untapped after attacking, so there's no defensive cost to attacking with it. With Phelia's attack trigger able to exile the only blocker (Voice of Victory), both creatures would get through unblocked for 6 total damage plus 4 life gained. Even without the exile, the Germ attacking forces the opponent to either take 4 damage or trade their Voice of Victory into it unfavorably.",
      "action_taken": "Only attacked with Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd, leaving the 4/4 vigilance lifelink Germ token back.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Phelia and the Batterskull-equipped Germ token. Use Phelia's trigger to exile Voice of Victory (the only blocker), getting through for 6 damage and gaining 4 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 71,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 114,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The opponent's only blue source is Tundra, and their Wasteland is tapped. This is the ideal window to play and activate Wasteland to destroy Tundra, cutting the opponent off blue mana (stranding Cryptic Coat which was tutored by Stoneforge Mystic). By playing Marsh Flats instead, ESPN gives the opponent time to untap their Wasteland and potentially retaliate or find another blue source.",
      "action_taken": "Played Marsh Flats as the land for the turn",
      "better_line": "Play Wasteland and immediately sacrifice it to destroy the opponent's Tundra, cutting them off blue mana while their own Wasteland is tapped and can't retaliate. ESPN already has enough mana sources (Karakas, Plateau, Sunbaked Canyon, Plains) to cast Amped Raptor.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 78,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 124,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "ESPN declined to use Karakas to bounce the opponent's Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd, a legendary creature that can blink ESPN's permanents and generate significant value. Karakas's bounce ability is essentially free (just a tap) and ESPN has enough other mana sources to cast Amped Raptor. Voice of Victory even prevents the opponent from responding during ESPN's turn, making this completely safe.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating any abilities, leaving Phelia on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Activate Karakas targeting Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd to return it to opponent's hand, forcing them to spend mana re-casting it and preventing it from attacking/blinking next turn. Then proceed to cast Amped Raptor using Plateau and another land.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 129,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Fetched Plateau over Elegant Parlor when ESPN already had sufficient untapped mana to cast Amped Raptor this turn. Elegant Parlor entering tapped wouldn't have cost tempo since ESPN had 4 other untapped lands plus a land drop from hand, and the surveil 1 trigger would have provided free card selection/filtering.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Plateau (untapped dual)",
      "better_line": "Fetch Elegant Parlor for the free surveil 1 trigger, since the tapped entry wouldn't have prevented casting Amped Raptor this turn anyway",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 129,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "ESPN could have activated Karakas to bounce Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd (a dangerous legendary creature that exiles permanents on attack) AND still cast Amped Raptor with the two untapped Plateaus. Karakas's bounce ability costs no mana - just tapping the land - and ESPN didn't need the {W} from Karakas for anything. Bouncing Phelia would force Sarge to re-spend 2 mana recasting it.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Amped Raptor without first using Karakas to bounce Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd.",
      "better_line": "Activate Karakas to return Phelia to opponent's hand (free tempo, no mana cost), then cast Amped Raptor with the two Plateaus.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 86,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 139,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "ESPN chose not to attack with Spirit Token (1/1 flyer) and Voice of Victory (1/3 with Mobilize 2) when the opponent has no untapped creatures that could block profitably. Stoneforge Mystic is untapped but only a 1/2, and Phelia is tapped. The Spirit Token flies so it can't be blocked at all. Voice of Victory creates two 1/1 attacking Warriors via Mobilize and prevents the opponent from casting spells during ESPN's turn, making combat tricks impossible. This would have dealt at least 4 damage (1 from Spirit + 1 from Voice + 2 from Warrior tokens) with minimal risk, putting the opponent from 15 to 11 life. The reasoning about 'Amped Raptors' appears confused and refers to cards not actually on the board.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped the attack phase entirely with no attackers declared.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Spirit Token and Voice of Victory. The Spirit Token is unblockable (flying), Voice of Victory prevents opponent from casting spells during your turn, and Mobilize creates additional attackers. This deals 4+ damage with very little risk.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 90,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 145,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The model's reasoning loop got stuck repeatedly calling pass_priority during the precombat main phase, failing to take any meaningful action. With Stoneforge Mystic untapped and Cryptic Coat in hand, the player should activate Stoneforge Mystic's ability to put Cryptic Coat onto the battlefield (cheating it into play for just {1}{W} instead of {2}{U}), which would cloak the top card and create an unblockable attacker. Alternatively, using Wasteland to destroy one of the opponent's nonbasic lands (Plateau) would be strong tempo. Passing without doing anything wastes the entire main phase.",
      "action_taken": "Repeatedly passed priority without taking any action during precombat main phase.",
      "better_line": "Activate Stoneforge Mystic's ability ({1}{W}, {T}) to put Cryptic Coat from hand onto the battlefield, creating a cloaked 2/2 unblockable creature equipped with Cryptic Coat (+1/+0). Then consider attacking with Phelia to exile an opponent's permanent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 91,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 148,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Attacking with Stoneforge Mystic risks it unnecessarily and taps it, preventing use of its activated ability ({1}{W}, {T}: put Equipment from hand onto battlefield) to deploy Cryptic Coat, Pre-War Formalwear, or Meteor Sword this turn. While Voice of Victory (1/3) can't kill it in combat, keeping Stoneforge back preserves the threat of activating it at instant speed during the opponent's turn or later this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with both Phelia and Stoneforge Mystic",
      "better_line": "Attack with only Phelia (3/3) to exile a permanent with her trigger, while keeping Stoneforge Mystic untapped to threaten activating its ability to deploy equipment (especially Cryptic Coat or Meteor Sword) at the optimal moment",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 93,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 154,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Phelia's attack trigger allows exiling an opponent's nonland permanent, which returns at end step with a +1/+1 counter on Phelia. The opponent has several high-value targets: Voice of Victory (which prevents the opponent from casting spells during your turn and creates attacking tokens), Staff of the Storyteller (card advantage engine), or Static Prison (which is imprisoning something). Instead, Sarge targeted their own Stoneforge Mystic to flicker it for an ETB re-trigger to search for equipment. While getting another equipment tutor has some value, Sarge already has Cryptic Coat, Pre-War Formalwear, and Meteor Sword in hand — they don't need more equipment. Meanwhile, Voice of Victory is a serious threat that creates tokens when attacking and prevents the opponent from casting spells during their turn, and Staff of the Storyteller is generating card advantage. Exiling Voice of Victory would remove a key threat and still give Phelia the +1/+1 counter since it returns under the opponent's control.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted own Stoneforge Mystic with Phelia's exile trigger to re-trigger its ETB for an equipment search.",
      "better_line": "Target Voice of Victory or Staff of the Storyteller with Phelia's exile trigger to temporarily remove a key opponent threat. Voice of Victory is particularly valuable to exile as it prevents opponent spellcasting during your turn and generates attacking tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 93,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 154,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Sarge passed priority during combat without using Wasteland to destroy one of ESPN's nonbasic lands (Plateau or Karakas). ESPN has tapped out (all four lands tapped), so there's no risk of interaction. Destroying a Plateau or Karakas would constrain ESPN's mana and options going forward. The Wasteland was available and there's no clear reason to save it. Additionally, Brainstorm could have been cast at instant speed to find better cards before the end step when Phelia's exile trigger resolves and Stoneforge Mystic re-enters.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat without activating Wasteland or casting Brainstorm.",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting ESPN's Karakas (to prevent bouncing Phelia) or a Plateau to constrain ESPN's mana. Could also cast Brainstorm to improve hand quality before Stoneforge re-enters at end step.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 93,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 154,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Sarge passed priority during combat without using Wasteland to destroy one of ESPN's nonbasic lands (Plateau or Karakas). ESPN's lands are all tapped, so destroying a nonbasic land would cost ESPN a key resource with no ability to respond meaningfully. Wasteland on ESPN's Karakas would be particularly valuable since it removes their ability to bounce Phelia (a legendary creature) in future turns, and ESPN's Karakas is already tapped so they can't use it in response. Alternatively, destroying a Plateau limits ESPN's colored mana. There's no reason to hold Wasteland here since Sarge has Karakas and Tundra for mana needs.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Wasteland during combat.",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting ESPN's Karakas (or a Plateau) to deny a critical resource while ESPN is tapped out.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 94,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 157,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Blocking Phelia (1/3) with a single Amped Raptor (2/1) results in the Raptor dying while Phelia survives (takes 2 of 3 toughness). This trades away a 2/1 first striker for nothing.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Phelia with a single Amped Raptor 2/1, which dies while Phelia survives at 1 remaining toughness.",
      "better_line": "Block with Voice of Victory (1/3), which results in a stalemate where neither creature dies (1 damage to each, both survive). Alternatively, block with two Amped Raptors to actually kill Phelia. Either line preserves more board presence.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 95,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 155,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd attacked into Voice of Victory (which creates two 1/1 Warrior tokens when attacking via Mobilize 2, but more importantly the opponent had Amped Raptor or first strike blockers available). The result was Phelia dying to 2 damage from Amped Raptor in combat. Before or during combat, Sarge had Karakas untapped and could have returned Phelia (a legendary creature) to hand to protect it, or could have used Wasteland to destroy a nonbasic land. More critically, during the combat step when given priority, Sarge passed rather than using Karakas to bounce Phelia back to safety after seeing blockers/combat damage assignments. Phelia is a key creature that was lost unnecessarily.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat, allowing Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd to die to Amped Raptor's 2 first strike damage.",
      "better_line": "Activate Karakas to return Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd to hand before damage, preserving the valuable legendary creature. Phelia could then be replayed next turn for another ETB trigger.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 95,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 158,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Sarge passed priority during combat without using Wasteland to destroy one of ESPN's nonbasic lands (Plateau or Karakas). ESPN has 4 lands (Karakas, 2x Plateau, Sunbaked Canyon, Plains) with several nonbasics that are valid targets. Destroying a Plateau or the opponent's Karakas would meaningfully constrain ESPN's mana while Sarge is behind on board and needs time to deploy equipment. The Wasteland is essentially a free resource since Sarge has no colorless mana requirements, and using it now (or at end of opponent's turn) is almost always correct when the opponent relies on nonbasic lands. Additionally, Sarge declined to cast Brainstorm, which could help find lands or better interaction given the hand is clogged with expensive equipment and no way to deploy them (only 3 lands, needing Stoneforge Mystic to cheat equipment into play but SFM is in hand, not on board).",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Wasteland or casting Brainstorm",
      "better_line": "Activate Wasteland targeting opponent's Karakas (or a Plateau) to constrain their mana development, and/or cast Brainstorm to dig for lands and improve hand quality",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 96,
      "player": "Gem3F Sarge",
      "decision_index": 159,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Sunbaked Canyon instead of Wasteland misses the opportunity to destroy the opponent's Tundra (their only blue mana source), which would cut off Cryptic Coat's bounce ability, future Dazes, and any blue spells. ESPN already has sufficient colored mana from Karakas, two Plateaus, and Plains to cast everything in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Played Sunbaked Canyon as land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Wasteland and use it to destroy opponent's Tundra, cutting off their blue mana while still having enough mana to cast Guide of Souls and Voice of Victory from existing lands.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 105,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 166,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "ESPN had 3 untapped mana (Karakas + 2 Plateaus) and could cast both Guide of Souls ({W}) and Voice of Victory ({1}{W}) this turn. By casting Voice of Victory first (2 mana), Guide of Souls should be cast first so it's on the battlefield when Voice of Victory's Mobilize 2 creates warrior tokens during combat, generating 2 life and 2 energy counters from those token entries.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Voice of Victory first for {1}{W}",
      "better_line": "Cast Guide of Souls first for {W}, then cast Voice of Victory for {1}{W}, so Guide of Souls triggers off the Mobilize warrior tokens during combat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "Gem25F ESPN",
      "decision_index": 168,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked a Warrior Token that would be sacrificed at end of step anyway (from Voice of Victory's Mobilize), instead of blocking an Amped Raptor (2/1) which is a permanent threat. Blocking the token only prevents 1 temporary damage while leaving three Amped Raptors dealing 6 total damage.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to block a 1/1 Warrior Token (which gets sacrificed at end of turn regardless)",
      "better_line": "Block an Amped Raptor (2/1) to trade Stoneforge Mystic for a permanent threat, since Sarge has another Stoneforge Mystic in hand and Pre-War Formalwear to recur creatures from graveyard",
      "type": "blunder",
